      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T07:03:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done for this comments. But I find that for uniform buffer emitting in hlsl backend, it change all types into uint4 arrays and using transform to replace all access words. I don\u0027t know why we do this and wonder whether \"push constant\" block should adopt the same rules. Would you mind to tell me more thing about this?",
      "parentUuid": "957bf1ea_52f4c9b0",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eff02f7b_5418bc05",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/printer/printer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T09:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, it seems that cbuffer requires a 16-byte row alignment. I think push constant also need this transforms.",
      "parentUuid": "f65f5bd8_89ad6cae",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6db480f8_55ca6a69",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/printer/printer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T09:41:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or meet wgsl alignment rule could also ensure we meet 16 byte row alignment in cbuffer?",
      "parentUuid": "eff02f7b_5418bc05",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d433d37_50847768",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/printer/printer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T13:38:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d guess it\u0027s better to update the `decompose_uniform_access` transform to also decompose push constants as it uses the same underlying `cbuffer` implementation.\n\nI can\u0027t remember the original reason for adding the transform @jrprice@google.com may remember? But we\u0027ve run into various issues with correctness and performance over the years which have been handled by decomposing the structures for HLSL.",
      "parentUuid": "6db480f8_55ca6a69",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2fe85cae_647d43cb",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/printer/printer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T15:17:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 16-byte field alignment is the main reason for that transform.\n\nAdding support for the `immediate` address space to `DecomposeUniformAccess` seems like a good approach. Alternatively you could run a separate transform beforehand the replaces `immediate` with `uniform` (and adds the binding point), and then nothing else after that has to handle the `immediate` address space at all.",
      "parentUuid": "4d433d37_50847768",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2991bb8_e2bc7c65",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/printer/printer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 3758334
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-24T01:41:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm... That might be a easy way (switch immediate data to uniform and left all nice and clean). I\u0027ll go to this approach with comment that ensure all validations happens before this transform and run it in raise after shaderIO transform and before Decompose uniform access transform. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "2fe85cae_647d43cb",
      "revId": "5cf41daaa3714bde9dbe87f7e5f018bf9aaa5541",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
